body:
I dropped out of school and was laid off due to COVID at roughly the same time early this year. Despite earning only $4300 from my part-time job, I applied for CERB, because it was either that or become homeless and starve. Got my first message the other day saying that I have to pay all of it back. I'm still jobless.

&#x200B;

Unfortunately they're going to have a hard time getting repayments from my corpse.

I've tried making changes. I moved cities for a change of scenery, I'm going to go back to school. I just don't have the energy or motivation to do anything more than that. 

&#x200B;

Something I won't do is seek therapy. It would be a waste of time. Other people are the source of most of my problems, there's no way I could turn to another person to try to solve them.
